  "title": "World's timekeepers upend how they adjust time to avoid catastrophic 'negative second'",
  "summary": "Governments have voted to abolish the leap second immediately and to replace it with a leap hour, aiming to avoid potential disruptions caused by the 'negative second' in global timekeeping.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Governments have voted to abolish the leap second immediately and to replace it with a leap hour",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The leap hour will replace the existing leap second, which is a critical component of timekeeping systems",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The decision aims to address potential issues with the current system and ensure accurate global time",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
